course: dictionary
lesson: 4022
title: A gateway is a way in
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gateway is an opening in a wall or fence, but the word also means a way into or through to somewhere else. The context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: «The walls helped control borders and trade, but enemies did get past: the Manchus came through the Shanhaiguan pass, a gateway in the Wall, in 1644.» Here the gateway is an opening in a huge wall, and people came through it. Pass and came through are your clues.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. «The Manchus came through the entrance in the Wall» still makes sense, so gateway means an entrance here.
explain: Gateway can also mean something that leads you to something bigger. «Reading is a gateway to learning» does not mean a gate you walk through. It means reading opens the door to lots more learning.
fact: A gateway is an opening in a wall or fence that can be shut with a gate. It is an entrance.
fact: «Dover is the gateway to France.» Here a gateway is a place you pass through to reach another place.
fact: «Reading is a gateway to learning.» Here a gateway is something that leads to something bigger.
fact: On a computer, a gateway is a device that connects one network to another.
fact: Useful phrases are «the gateway to» and «stand in the gateway». Look for clues like pass through, reach, or leads to.
exercise: «The walls helped control borders and trade, but enemies did get past: the Manchus came through the Shanhaiguan pass, a gateway in the Wall, in 1644.» In this sentence, what is a gateway? | A soldier who guards the top of the wall | A long road that runs around the wall | A thick layer of stone | *An opening in the Wall that people could pass through
exercise: Mia says «Dover is the gateway to France» means Dover is a high wall around France. What does gateway mean here? | A kind of gate for cars only | A high wall that keeps France safe | A famous French dinner | *A place you pass through to reach France
exercise: «Reading is a gateway to learning.» What does gateway suggest? | A place to sit and rest | A type of computer | A metal gate that stops you going in | *Something that leads you to something bigger
test: On a computer, what is a gateway? | A game played on a screen | A type of keyboard | *A device that connects one network to another | The button that turns the computer on
test: Which word fits the gap? The old ___ in the garden wall was shut with a wooden gate. | *gateway | river | mountain | cloud
exam: Which sentence uses gateway to mean something that leads to something bigger? | The old gateway in the wall was painted red. | We walked through the gateway to the park. | *Learning to read can be a gateway to every other subject.
